// Package editor implements the NSGo Scene Editor over packages/game/sceneformat.
//
// It provides:
//   - Command-pattern undo/redo history (History, Command) covering every scene edit.
//   - Scene document loading, saving, object placement, selection, transform editing,
//     and deletion (Editor, PlaceObject, MoveObject, RotateObject, ScaleObject, DeleteObject).
//   - Inline tilemap editing with paint, erase, BFS flood fill, autotiled Terrain brush painting (PaintTile, EraseTile, FloodFillTile, PaintTerrain, EraseTerrain, ToolTerrain, TileStrokeTerrain, TileStrokeEraseTerrain), rectangle, Bresenham line, stamp (with palette rectangle selection and map region copy/cut/paste), and deterministic seeded weighted random brushes with live viewport preview, Escape cancel, and single-step undo (FillTileRect, DrawTileLine, StampTiles, CopyTileRegion, CutTileRegion, PasteTileRegion, BeginTileStroke), paired with a docked Tileset Editor for defining 4-bit cardinal and 8-bit blob terrain sets and assigning tiles to neighbor bitmasks by clicking edges and corners (OpenTilesetFile, OpenActiveLayerTileset, AddTilesetTerrain, ToggleTilesetEdgeOrCorner, TilesetEditorPanelView).
//   - A layers panel that picks the active layer and adds, removes, renames, reorders, hides and locks layers, each edit but the session's lock undoable (Layers, AddLayer, RemoveLayer, RenameLayer, MoveLayer, SetLayerVisible, SetLayerSpace, SetLayerLocked, LayersView), paired with undoable layer parallax and repeat editing in the inspector (SetLayerParallax, SetLayerRepeat) and live parallax/repeat preview in the 2D viewport.
//   - Typed property, component, and scene settings inspection and editing (SetProperty, SetComponentField, SetSceneName, SetVirtualSize, SetBackground, SetCamera, SetCameraPosition, SetCameraZoom, SetCameraRotation, SetCameraBounds, ClearCameraBounds, InspectorView), including draggable 2D camera position and camera.bounds resize/move handles when scene settings are active, and side-by-side *.rooms.yaml room-map editing in the 2D viewport with tile-grid snapping and room inspection (OpenRoomsFile, NewRoomMap, AddRoom, DeleteRoom, SetRoomRect, SetRoomID, SetRoomName, SetRoomTransition, SaveRoomsFile).
//   - Play-in-editor preview powered by game.Loop with exact pre-play YAML snapshot restoration (Play, PlayIn, Stop).
//   - An animation editor that keys any registered property on a timeline, previews the clip with animclip and saves it as an animation resource file (NewClip, KeyProperty, SeekClip, PlayClip, SaveClipFile, AnimationPanelView).
//   - A Data Table editor that opens versioned datatable YAML files from the file browser as a sortable, filterable grid with inferred value kinds, undo/redo, lossless round-trip saves and optional per-pattern Go row-type validation (OpenDataTableFile, RegisterDataTableType, SetDataTableCellText, DataTablePanelView).
//   - Atlas asset browsing and drop-to-place sprite creation (Assets, DropAtlasFrame, AssetBrowserView).
//   - Placing models in 3D: the asset browser lists the built-in primitives and the project's glTF models with thumbnails rendered offscreen, and the Place tool, a drag from the browser or a .glb dropped from another app adds an object drawing one where the pointer's ray meets the scene's geometry or the ground plane, optionally snapped to the grid and aligned to the surface, as one undoable step; the 3D inspector's Model field picks a project model (Models, ModelThumbnail, SelectModel, PlacementAt3D, PlaceModel3D, PlaceModelAt3D, DropModelFiles, SetObjectModel).
//   - Projects that bring their own assets: with ProjectAssets set, an opened project's scenes draw its atlases, the asset browser lists them and its scene files place as instances, through a project.Resolver over its directory, and OpenProjectScene opens a project on any of its scenes (ProjectAssets, OpenProjectScene; package editorcmd is the command line that sets them up).
//   - Editor plugins built into the editor binary and turned on by the project's game.yaml, which add docked panels, inspectors for their component types, 2D and 3D viewport tools (with camera pick ray and 3D projection overlays via Press3D, Draw3D, OnDragBegin3D/Move3D/End3D/Cancel3D, OnHover3D), and per-component 3D gizmos with object-space point/line/box handles that commit as one undo step (Plugin, ComponentGizmo3D, GizmoHandle3D, Projection3D, RegisterPlugin, SetPluginEnabled).
//   - A file browser that lists the open project's files and moves or renames them with every reference to them rewritten, on disk and in the open scene and project, as one undoable step (ProjectFiles, MoveFile through package refs, FilesView).
//   - A Project Settings panel over game.yaml editing general metadata, window, display, autoload scenes/resources and main scene, and editor plugins through EditProject with inline validation errors, canonical-save notice, undo/redo, and synced nsgo.yaml saving (ProjectSettingsPanelView, SetProjectSettingsOpen).
//   - A 2D viewport that pans, zooms and frames through the editor's own view, separate from the scene's camera, whose frame it outlines (View2D, PanView2D, ZoomView2DAt, FrameSelection2D, FrameAll2D, ResetView2D).
//   - A 2D transform gizmo that drags an object to move it, keeping the grab offset, moves it along its own axes, turns it with a ring and scales it with corner and edge handles (Shift keeps the aspect ratio), each drag one undoable step that Escape or a cancelled gesture puts back (BeginDrag2D, UpdateDrag2D, EndDrag2D, CancelDrag2D, PickGizmo2D).
//   - Interactive 2D viewport shape handles for registered point, rect, circle and polygon component fields (with a ShowAllShapes toggle, optional SnapToGrid snapping, polygon vertex add/remove, and undoable SetComponentField commits via BeginShapeDrag2D, UpdateShapeDrag2D, EndShapeDrag2D, CancelShapeDrag2D, AddPolygonVertex, RemovePolygonVertex), plus drag (OnDragBegin, OnDragMove, OnDragEnd, OnDragCancel) and hover (OnHover) callbacks on PluginTool.
//   - An audio bus mixer over game.yaml's audio section with undoable bus and effect-chain editing and live audition through sound.Mixer (AudioMixerPanelView, AddAudioBus, AddAudioBusEffect, AuditionAudioBus).
//   - A Problems panel that runs assetcheck.CheckWith (with the editor's component registry) and project.Check over the open project off the UI goroutine on open, save and file move, shows one row per problem with file, line and message, navigates to scenes or selects files on press, and displays the live problem count in the status bar (CheckProblems, Problems, OpenProblem, ProblemsView).
//   - An Export & Release panel over game.yaml's export section with undoable preset and target editing, pre-flight asset credits verification, streaming dry-run and release builds, and automatic output folder opening (ExportPanelView, AddExportPreset, CheckExportCredits, StartExportBuild), plus a full-window Build and Release screen (BuildReleaseScreenView, OpenBuildReleaseScreen, CloseBuildReleaseScreen, BuildReleaseScreenOpen, StartReleaseBuild, StopReleaseBuild, ResumeReleaseBuild, SetBuildPresetIncluded, SetBuildPresetFixProposal, ApplyBuildPresetFixAndRebuild) showing BEFORE EVERY BUILD checks (`nsgo check`, smoke playtest, and `game.yaml` budgets), per-preset ordered steps (`Check project`, `Compile Go`, `Pack assets`, `Sign`, `Smoke playtest`, `Measure`) with `build/<platform>.log` streaming, failure isolation with agent preset fix diffs, finished size breakdowns against the last release, and platform readiness checks.
//   - Project-wide Search and Find References covering file names and paths, file UIDs, scene object IDs and names, component types, and prefab/scene references, plus incoming file references powered by refs.Scan with file and line numbers and jump-to-file/scene-object navigation (Search, FindReferences, ShowReferences, OpenSearchResult, OpenReference, RefreshSearch, SearchPanelView).
//   - Running the open project with `go tool game dev` (optionally starting at the open scene or with `-automation`) from the toolbar or F5 shortcut with full process-tree cleanup on Stop, paired with a docked Output / Log panel that streams stdout and stderr, keeps a timestamped history of editor status and error messages, supports Clear and Errors-only filtering, and opens clicked `file:line` scene links (RunGame, RunGameWith, StopGame, Close, OutputPanelView, OpenOutputEntry).
//   - A Remote scene tree tab and live inspector connected to the running game over MCP (`go tool nsgo mcp` or an injected transport via `github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/mcp`), listing live scenes, layers, and entities with hierarchy (`game_scenes_list`, `game_layers_list`, `game_entities_list`), inspecting and editing live components (`game_entity_inspect`, `game_component_set`) with tracked Live Changes that can be reverted, discarded, or kept in the open scene as a single undo step, plus live Pause/Resume/Step N/Time Scale controls (`game_loop_*`), tunables (`game_tunable_*`), and a debug console line (`game_console_exec`) (ConnectRemote, ConnectRemoteCommand, DisconnectRemote, RefreshRemote, SelectRemoteEntity, SetRemoteComponentField, KeepRemoteLiveChangesInScene, DiscardRemoteLiveChanges, RemotePause, RemoteResume, RemoteStep, RemoteSetTimeScale, RemoteSetTunable, RemoteExecConsole, NewRemoteBridgeServer).
//   - A Profiler for the running game: a Play-mode "FRAME TIME · LAST 60 S" strip under the viewport (ProfilerStripView) showing avg, p99, allocs/frame, 8.3 ms / 16.7 ms thresholds, time axis and labelled spikes, plus a full docked Profiler panel (ProfilerPanelView) opened from the strip, toolbar or command registry that polls game_perf_readout and game_perf_zones over MCP (ConnectProfiler, ConnectProfilerMCP, ConnectProfilerCommand, ConnectProfilerScope, PollProfiler), charts frame/update/draw time, FPS, allocations/GC and asset memory, lists zones sorted by cost with Reset (game_perf_reset), and exports recorded frames as Chrome/Perfetto trace JSON through debug.Profiler.WriteChromeTrace (ExportProfilerTrace, ExportProfilerTraceFile).
//   - A unified command registry driving platform-aware keyboard shortcuts (guarded against firing while text fields have focus), a desktop application menu bar (File, Edit, View, Project), a searchable Command Palette (ui.CommandDialog) covering built-in commands, plugin commands, plugin tools, plugin panels and project scenes/files, and clash-checked plugin command registration (EditorCommand, PluginCommand, RegisterCommand, ApplicationMenu, CommandPaletteView).
//   - Scene tabs and scene files: a tab bar above the viewport (SceneTabsView) keeping each open scene's document, undo/redo history, selection, 2D/3D view transform and dirty marker separate while sharing the project file across tabs (Tabs, ActiveTab, TabCount, SelectTab, SaveTab, CloseTab, RequestCloseTab, OpenInstancedScene, OpenBaseScene); opening an already-open scene switches to its tab, saving a scene rebuilds other open tabs that instance or inherit it, closing a dirty tab prompts to save, discard or cancel, and New Scene, Save As and Revert operate on scenes (OpenScene, NewScene, SaveSceneAs, RevertScene, SceneDirty, AnySceneDirty, HasUnsavedChanges, Save, SaveAll).
//   - Asset import settings inspection and rebuilding: selecting an image, sound, font, or 3D model in the file browser displays its kind-specific import settings (inheriting target defaults from game.yaml with per-field Reset), an interactive image slice-grid preview with draggable default and per-cell pivot markers, and the credit section in the inspector, writes validated *.import.yaml sidecars through importsettings.Encode as undoable steps, and runs `go tool game assets` via Reimport or Build Assets off the UI goroutine with Output panel streaming and live atlas/texture reloading in the asset browser and viewport (InspectAssetImport, EditAssetImportSettings, SetImageImportPivot, SetImageImportDefaultPivot, SetImageImportCellPivot, BeginImagePivotDrag, DrawImageImportPreview, SetAssetImportCredit, ResetAssetImportField, ReimportAsset, BuildAssets, ReloadAssets).
//   - A Start Screen (StartScreenView) with per-user strict versioned YAML recent projects persistence (RecentProjects, ParseRecentProjects, EncodeRecentProjects, DefaultRecentProjectsPath) marking missing folders, folder-picker opening (BrowseAndOpenProject, PickProjectFolder), dynamic template gallery and `game new` project creation with live name validation and streaming output (ProjectTemplates, StartCreateProject), Open Demo (OpenDemo, NewDemo), and clean project switching with unsaved-edits confirmation (HasUnsavedChanges, RequestOpenProject, ConfirmSaveAndSwitch, ConfirmDiscardAndSwitch).
//   - Localized editor UI (English and Simplified Chinese via embedded versioned l10n YAML catalogs) with live language switching without restart, plugin translation catalogs (Plugin.Catalog, Plugin.LocaleYAML, Editor.PluginT, Editor.PluginPlural), and per-user versioned YAML Editor Settings (language and light/dark/system appearance via core.Scope.SetAppearance) stored outside any project (EditorSettings, ParseEditorSettings, EncodeEditorSettings, Editor.LoadSettings, Editor.SetLanguage, Editor.SetAppearance, EditorSettingsDialogView).
//   - A HUD and menu layout screen (HUDLayoutView, OpenHUDScreen, OpenHUDScreenFile, OpenHUDScreenDoc) that previews every *.screen.yaml file simultaneously across Phone 19.5:9 with notch, Tablet 4:3, Desktop 16:9 and Ultrawide 21:9 in any project language (SetHUDLocale), displays Safe areas / Anchors / Touch areas / Focus order overlays, compares localized widths in a TEXT WIDTH, PX table, inspects anchors (3×3 grid plus fill), safe-area placement, Fixed / Fit text sizing, localized text with 1.5× overflow zoom, and live GAME CHECK diagnostics backed by gameui.CheckScreen, and supports undoable container reordering, spacing edits, and direct touch-control dragging written back to the screen file in one undo step.
//   - Object-by-object scene merge conflict resolution (MergeConflictView, OpenMergeConflict, OpenMergeConflictSession, ResolveMergeConflict, TakeAllAgentMergeSuggestions, ApplyMergeCustomYAML, FinishMerge, AbortMerge) displaying MINE, THEIRS, and live RESULT scene previews, auto-merged items (MERGED BY ID), per-object Agent/Mine/Theirs options with reasons, hand YAML editing, game check and short playtest verification, Git merge commit creation, and clean merge abort.
//   - A native NSGo UI root view (EditorView) combining the start screen, scene merge conflict resolver, HUD layout screen, toolbar, asset browser, file browser, interactive canvas viewport, property inspector, search & references panel, problems panel, export panel, output panel, command palette, unsaved-edits dialog, editor settings dialog, and the plugins' panels.
package editor
